        <Dialogs>
          <Dialog>○○○○○○○○</Dialog>
          <Dialog>(I've only called, but they
accepted my application right
away.)</Dialog>
          <Dialog>(I guess they're really
short-handed in spring...)</Dialog>
          <Dialog>(Family Restaurant "Dixie's".
I'll be working here from
today on, huh...？)</Dialog>
          <Dialog>All right then... What should
I do first？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>？？？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Welcome！</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Just one, sir？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>(Whoa, she's beautiful. She
looks so mature, is she in
college？ Wait, not that！)</Dialog>
          <Dialog>How may I help you？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Um... I will be working
part-time here from today
on...</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Eh？ Ah, are you a new
employee？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Yes.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Please come here.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Employees are not allowed to
use the customers' entrance,
you know？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>I'm sorry...</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Hehe, it's all right. After
all, it's your first day.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Anegasaki</Dialog>
          <Dialog>I'm Nene Anegasaki. Nice to
meet you？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>I'm ▲苗字▲ ▲名前▲.
Nice to meet you.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>I guess I'm a year ahead of
you, both here and at
school？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>In school...？ But, I have
just transferred here. How do
you...</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Hehe. Sorry, I heard from the
manager that a junior from my
high school would come to work
here.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Ah, is that so？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Hmm～... that's a little
stiff, isn't it？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>What is？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>The polite speech. We're
only one year apart, so it
feels like you're treating
me as way older, and that's
a little, you know.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Sor... I mean, sorry. I'm a
little nervous.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Yes, like that. But use
polite speech with
customers, okay？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Our restaurant is strict
about that. Okay？</Dialog>
          <Dialog>I underst... I mean, okay.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Hehe. Alright, I'm heading
back for now. Can you wait
here？ The manager should be
here soon.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Okay, thanks.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>Hehe, you're welcome.</Dialog>
          <Dialog>(Looks like this part-time job
will be fun...)</Dialog>
        </Dialogs>
      </SDL2>
